                <pb facs="0683" n="599" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg599"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">uneasy feeling among the northeastern tribes
                        increasing.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Saint Paul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi>
                        5</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>A telegram from Ada Mina states: The Indians of Red Lake Reservation present an
                    alarming aspect. It has been learned that for some time they have been gathering
                    arms, ammunition, and horses in the surrounding country. It is feared that they
                    have been excited by emissaries from the northwest.</p>
            </div>
